<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2013/Fiddlers-Green-Sketch.jpg" alt="This small plein air painting of a white silo and barn was done mainly with a painting knife." width="400" height="348" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Silo at Little Fiddler's Green. &nbsp;5x7 oil on linen. 2013</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Here's another small sketch I did on location, this one at Little Fiddler's Green. &nbsp;It's less finished than the one shown in the previous post.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">More than anything else I was trying to capture the color of the shadow areas of the barn and silo. &nbsp;In photographs I took the same day those areas look almost black and not at all as they appear in real life - warm and cool grays filled with reflected light.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The tree was painted with thick paint using a palette knife.</p>